Number messages evaluate arithmetic, comparisons, numeric conversions, bitwise
operations, predicates and range/block iteration locally. Unary math includes
square root, powers, logarithms, trigonometry, factorial and rounding.
Division, integer division and remainder require one nonzero numeric divisor;
reciprocal requires a nonzero receiver. Invalid divisors signal a numeric error.
Missing methods fall back to loaded Number class methods; remaining unsupported
messages signal with the receiver and selector instead of returning nil.
